    {
      "id": "claim_0fda545a69d64a2cad1b54829d5621d3",
      "statement": "There is no deferred-creation queue, retry, dirty flag or conflict detection anywhere in the roster sync path, so a locally created roster stays local-only forever even after a working token appears: the only route that could create a server row (POST /rosters) is never replayed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/src/lib/api.ts#L285-L386",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31b160f184418f6c7df8d033e99693d465099d395edeb13835ec3de71ef62d45:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2331574f36f451590096fe2bee620cf",
      "statement": "Every roster handler is mounted behind requireAuth and restates ownership inline: GET /rosters uses findMany on userId, GET/:id uses findFirst({id, userId}), POST stamps userId from the token rather than the body, and PUT/DELETE use findFirst({id, userId}) as a guard before mutating by id alone, answering 404 NOT_FOUND (never 403) for foreign or unknown ids.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/routes/rosters.ts#L16-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd3fb7378b29cf70dddb8d8d6d0ee05b5fe85a79f33e98dde50c5352bbc78df6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88568af920c9463199b0ba4656ce533b",
      "statement": "POST /rosters keeps rulesetVersionId server-controlled at 11.1.0-2026-Q3 and defaults rosterPayload to { units: [], totalPoints: 0, detachmentPointsUsed: 0 }, so client-supplied ruleset versions are ignored on create.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/routes/rosters.ts#L56-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24c0d99ea61ce32eb5999f53b07ef45a70d21c538aa600a4177cd62f37f2b022:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ef5a8d171c8e4033824535b63e3a6727",
      "statement": "The PUT handler's update object is asymmetric: name, detachmentPrimary, pointsLimit and rosterPayload fall back to the guard snapshot with ?? existing, while detachmentSecondary and factionThemeOverride are forwarded straight from the body, so omitting them leaves the columns untouched but sending them as null clears them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/routes/rosters.ts#L106-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4747e87363572eff0227486691ad47620246f483b201eac8d6ebafb897b2fd01:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3ad1e835fa74d51b2ad9d744743cdab",
      "statement": "Roster writes are last-write-wins at whole-rosterPayload granularity: no optimistic concurrency token, revision counter, ETag or updatedAt precondition exists on either side, the PUT updates unconditionally after its guard read, and roster_payload is a single JSONB column always replaced whole by the client.",
